it describes an election held on 2026-11-03.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. OFFICIAL AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL — not ours to license
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Ballot text, measure digests, candidate statements and designations are
  public records published by the California Secretary of State and the
  Registrars of Voters for San Francisco, Alameda, San Mateo and Contra Costa
  counties. They are reproduced here as public records. Candidate contact
  email addresses have been redacted (see `tools/redact.py`).
- Campaign-finance figures derive from SF Ethics (DataSF), Cal-Access
  (CA SoS), the FEC, and NetFile — all public disclosure data.
- Other organisations' endorsements in `site/data/endorsements.json` and
  `site/data/picks.json`'s comparison columns are those organisations'
  positions, cited to their own published guides. They are quoted for
  comparison and remain theirs.
- `site/css/{tokens,landing,subpage}.css` and `site/js/palette.js` are copied
  from the congress_trader frontend (same author, MIT).
